WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.110
Passive network telemetry often gives hunters broad visibility without actively querying sensitive devices.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:11.658
It can show assets, peers, protocols, timing, and communication across trust boundaries.

00:00:11.658 --> 00:00:15.818
Protocol-aware sources may add sessions, reads, writes, commands, errors,

00:00:15.818 --> 00:00:17.205
or engineering operations.

00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:21.828
Firewall, VPN, jump-host, and vendor-access logs describe boundary connections, identities,

00:00:21.828 --> 00:00:25.064
source systems, approvals, destinations, and session duration.

00:00:25.064 --> 00:00:29.687
HMI and engineering-workstation records may add logons, processes, project access,

00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:33.386
file activity, removable media, and connections to controllers.

00:00:33.386 --> 00:00:37.084
Historian data connects cyber observations to physical behavior.

00:00:37.084 --> 00:00:38.471
Trends, alarms, setpoints,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:44.943
and equipment state can show whether a technical event coincided with an operational change.

00:00:44.943 --> 00:00:50.491
Authentication events add account lifecycle, failed access, privilege, and unusual user timing.

00:00:50.491 --> 00:00:55.576
Controller change records, project repositories, and management tools may report downloads,

00:00:55.576 --> 00:00:58.812
mode changes, firmware work, or configuration differences.

00:00:58.812 --> 00:01:04.360
These records are valuable when network traffic is encrypted or when the

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.671
hunt concerns local engineering activity.

00:01:06.671 --> 00:01:08.983
Every source has blind spots.

00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:14.068
Passive sensors miss unobserved segments, serial devices behind gateways, dormant assets,

00:01:14.068 --> 00:01:15.455
and local actions.

00:01:15.455 --> 00:01:17.767
Endpoint logging may be incomplete.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:22.390
Historians may show an effect without identifying who initiated it.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.088
Inconsistent clocks or asset names make correlation unreliable.

00:01:26.088 --> 00:01:30.249
Before hunting, document coverage, time synchronization, retention, field quality,

00:01:30.249 --> 00:01:31.636
and source ownership.

00:01:31.636 --> 00:01:34.872
Protect sensitive telemetry and preserve original evidence.

00:01:34.872 --> 00:01:41.344
A strong hunt combines complementary sources, states what the data can and cannot prove,

00:01:41.344 --> 00:01:44.580
and adjusts confidence when visibility is incomplete.
